<title>USA: Allegheny Teledyne settles U.S. disputes.</title>
<headline>Allegheny Teledyne settles U.S. disputes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teledyne Industries Inc., a unit of Allegheny Teledyne, will pay the U.S. government $11.5 million to settle two disputes involving defense contracts, the Justice Department said on Monday.</p>
<p>The first case, settled for $4.75 million, involves allegations that Teledyne defrauded the government by failing to account for engine aircraft parts used to repair U.S. Air Force jets at 15 bases.</p>
<p>The other $6.75 million payment settled a claim that its Teledyne Thermatics unit failed to test wire and cable as required by its defense contract, the department said.</p>
</text>
